Subject: Add foundational monomorphic property inline caches

What this does
  Caches repeated own-property reads, direct prototype reads, writable
  overwrites and add-transition stores. The shipping configuration keeps one
  entry per site, with an optional two-entry configuration for experiments.
  Cache tables are allocated only when a site fills successfully, and a site
  that becomes megamorphic skips further refill work.

Why we need it
  React Native repeatedly initializes and reads fields on objects with stable
  shapes. Without these caches, each access repeats generic shape and property
  lookup work. The transition-store path is the demonstrated win on this
  runtime; read results are retained as a faithful foundational implementation
  and are measured separately.

What it adds
  get_field_ic()   - reads an own or direct-prototype data property by shape.
  get_field2_ic()  - reads a property while preserving its receiver value.
  put_field_ic()   - handles writable overwrites and add-transition stores.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes. The opcode set and serialized IC metadata changed; the version bump is
  kept in 9999-bc-version-bump.patch.
